-- title:
--   Original finite-mark signed source-rate uniform floor and stopped real-time kernels are jointly strongly measurable
-- statement:
--   For the original true no-physical-jump BV Lévy source and actual admissible right-dividend strategy, show that the inclusive capped negative-mark rate sampled at the strict physical uniform-floor cells, the continuous stopped real-time rate, and the mapped nonnegative-time rate are strongly measurable under their original finite-horizon Lebesgue clocks. This retains the literal original time, ruin and zero/cap contact masks.
-- source:
--   Proved 1816332a original prepayment leftlimit joint measurability, d8a9025e original finite clock left reserve measurable, d7d02797 original negative-mark stopped rate, d581abf8 real-floor simple-step measurability; Avram (2007) Prop4(i),(5.13).

import Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.ContDiff.Defs
import Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.Exponential
